#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""qcon - ONE console session per guest over the XEN PV CONSOLE: open, run, run, ..., close.

THE OWNER'S RULE (2026-09-17, verbatim): "the proper way to use console is attach once and pray it
won't break!" and "YOU HAVE MORE THAN ONE ATTACH?"  So: EXACTLY ONE attach per guest per session.
`open` attaches once, wakes the pty, logs in and KEEPS that session in a detached background
process; every `run` types its command through that one session; `close` ends it. A second attach
while a session exists is REFUSED and names who holds it; `run` without an open session is REFUSED
(there is no implicit attach). If the session goes silent, that silence is information - the tool
reports it and LEAVES THE SESSION OPEN; it never re-attaches to "check".

WHY IT WAS REBUILT (2026-09-17). The previous design attached PER INVOCATION: a `--raw` probe was
one attach, the login another, every command another. The console admits ONE attacher (see below),
and on every stalled guest for a month the transcript had the same shape - a login prompt, then
nothing after the username, then nothing on every later attach. That was written up as guest death
ten times (specimen 10: seven attaches in thirty minutes, the first a raw probe). Owner: "every
time you claim you see a console, and then say 'it is not answering username anymore' something in
your console access procedure is deeply broken, either it is unidirectional or locking or there is
something else that goes wrong." The per-attach design is the named defect; this file removes it.
Whether the second attach dies from a stale lock, a pty split or something else is UNTESTED - what
is measured is only that later attaches returned nothing, and the fake in the self-test models
exactly that observable and nothing more.

WHY THIS EXISTS (unchanged). Every other way this qube reaches a guest goes through the guest's own
qrexec agent (tools/qtest run/ps/push/pushrun), so all of them die together in the failure class
this project keeps hitting: "guest alive, qrexec dead". The PV console rides a different transport
entirely - xenbus's console ring + evtchn, serviced by dom0's xenconsoled, terminated in the guest
by xencons.sys -> xencons_monitor -> xencons_tty -> cmd.exe. It shares no code, no service and no
user session with qrexec.

WHAT STILL HAS TO BE ALIVE (this is NOT "works on any dead guest"):
  - THIS qube's qrexec to dom0. admin.vm.Console is itself a qrexec call; what it does not need is
    the GUEST's qrexec agent. dom0 opens the guest's console pty locally.
  - the guest's xencons driver and its worker. A guest deadlocked at high IRQL silences this too.
  - policy: admin.vm.Console for this qube (dom0/12-install-policy-tagged.sh).

ONE ATTACHER AT A TIME. dom0's `xl console` and this tool open the same pty slave and split the
byte stream, so a concurrent attach returns nothing. admin.vm.Console's dom0 script also takes
`flock -n -E 200`, so a second attacher - including a stale lock left by a killed client - exits
200 (reported as BUSY), and a qrexec policy refusal exits 126 (REFUSED). NOCONSOLE (no bytes, not
even dom0's [ATTACHED] banner) is inconclusive and is never "the guest is dead".

THE SIGNAL NET (77344ef, kept). Wrapping the old qcon in `timeout` sent SIGTERM to the python,
which exited WITHOUT unwinding, so the qrexec-client-vm child was orphaned STILL ATTACHED and every
later attach was silent - three runs were written up as the guest losing its console. Signals are
turned into SystemExit here so `finally` always runs, in the client and in the session daemon.

Usage:
    tools/qcon open   <vm> [--user U --pass P]      # attach ONCE, wake, log in, keep the session
    tools/qcon run    <vm> [--deadline S --stall S] '<command>'
    tools/qcon login  <vm> --user U [--pass P]      # finish a login through the OPEN session
    tools/qcon status <vm>                          # open? age, phase, last activity
    tools/qcon shell  <vm> [--user U --pass P]      # open if needed, then interactive passthrough
    tools/qcon close  <vm> [--logout]               # end the session (--logout types `exit` first)
    tools/qcon <vm> '<command>'                     # convenience: open + run + close, ONE attach;
                                                    # refused while a session for <vm> exists
Environment:
    QCON_USER / QCON_PASS       credentials when --user/--pass are not given
    QCON_DEADLINE (45) / QCON_STALL (12)   per-command budget: total seconds / silent seconds
    QCON_LOGIN_DEADLINE (45)    a Windows login takes seconds; be generous
    QCON_QUIET (1.5)            silence that counts as "the previous exchange is over"
    QCON_BUDGET (600)           wall clock for ONE client invocation (never wrap qcon in `timeout`)
    QCON_STATE_ROOT ($HOME/tmp) session state lives in <root>/qcon-<vm>/ ; every attach and detach
                                is appended to <root>/qcon-attach-ledger.log with a timestamp
    QCON_TRANSPORT (qrexec)     `fake:<unix socket>` replaces ONLY the attach primitive (self-test)
    QCON_DEFECT                 `perattach` re-introduces the OLD attach-per-command behaviour so
                                the self-test can be seen to FAIL on it. Never set it for real.
State dir (<root>/qcon-<vm>/): pid, sock, state.json, attach.log, session.log (raw transcript),
daemon.log. `close` moves session.log to <root>/qcon-<vm>.closed.log and removes the dir.

Exit codes: 0 ok / 1 usage / 2 NOCONSOLE / 3 NEEDS_LOGIN / 4 guest not running / 5 no output
within the budget (session left open) / 6 BUSY (another attacher) / 7 REFUSED by policy /
8 no session open / 9 a session already exists (open refused).

Self-test (offline, fake console): tools/tests/qcon-session-selftest.sh
"""
import codecs
import json
import os
import select
import shutil
import signal
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import time

DEADLINE = float(os.environ.get("QCON_DEADLINE", "45"))
STALL = float(os.environ.get("QCON_STALL", "12"))
QUIET = float(os.environ.get("QCON_QUIET", "1.5"))
LOGIN_DEADLINE = float(os.environ.get("QCON_LOGIN_DEADLINE", "45"))
BUDGET = float(os.environ.get("QCON_BUDGET", "600"))
STATE_ROOT = os.environ.get("QCON_STATE_ROOT") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "tmp")
TRANSPORT = os.environ.get("QCON_TRANSPORT", "qrexec")
DEFECT = os.environ.get("QCON_DEFECT", "")

RC_OK, RC_USAGE, RC_NOCONSOLE, RC_NEEDS_LOGIN, RC_NOT_RUNNING = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4
RC_NO_OUTPUT, RC_BUSY, RC_REFUSED, RC_NO_SESSION, RC_SESSION_EXISTS = 5, 6, 7, 8, 9

BUF_CAP = 256 * 1024


def ts():
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S", time.gmtime()) + "Z"


def say(op, msg):
    """Every line this tool prints says which of open/run/login/status/shell/close it is in."""
    print(f"qcon {op}: {msg}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def _install_signal_net(budget):
    """Signals become SystemExit so every `finally` runs (77344ef). See the header."""
    def bye(sig, _frame):
        raise SystemExit(128 + sig)
    for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGALRM):
        try:
            signal.signal(s, bye)
        except (ValueError, OSError):
            pass
    # alarm(0) CANCELS. Arming only when budget>0 left an INHERITED alarm live: the client arms
    # signal.alarm(QCON_BUDGET) in __main__, the detached session daemon inherits it, and the
    # daemon's _install_signal_net(0) never cleared it - so every session died exactly QCON_BUDGET
    # seconds after `open` with reason='signal/exit 142'. Measured on the first live run,
    # 2026-09-17 (ATTACH 11:09:38Z -> DETACH 11:19:38Z, 600.0 s, guest healthy throughout).
    if os.environ.get("QCON_DEFECT") == "alarm" and budget <= 0:   # GUARD:alarm (self-test knob)
        return
    try:
        signal.alarm(int(budget) if budget > 0 else 0)
    except (ValueError, OSError):
        pass


def vm_running(vm):
    """Terminal-state check: a halted guest can never produce a console. TRANSIENT COUNTS AS
    RUNNING - Qubes reports Transient while waiting for the GUEST'S QREXEC, which is exactly the
    "guest alive, qrexec dead" case this tool exists for (measured 2026-09-09, four attempts)."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["qvm-ls", "--raw-data", "--fields", "NAME,STATE"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60).stdout
    except Exception:
        return None                      # unknown - do not claim a terminal state
    for line in out.splitlines():
        parts = line.split("|")
        if len(parts) >= 2 and parts[0] == vm:
            return parts[1] in ("Running", "Transient")
    return False


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- the ONE attach
class ConsoleGone(Exception):
    pass


class Console:
    """One attach. The transport is the only thing QCON_TRANSPORT replaces; reading, writing,
    pumping and syncing are the shipped code on both transports."""

    def __init__(self, vm, transcript=None):
        self.vm, self.buf, self.eof = vm, b"", False
        self.rx_bytes, self.last_rx, self.transcript = 0, None, transcript
        self.attached_at = time.time()
        if TRANSPORT.startswith("fake:"):
            self.p = None
            self.sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
            self.sock.connect(TRANSPORT[5:])
            self.rfd = self.wfd = self.sock.fileno()
            self.how = f"fake:{TRANSPORT[5:]}"
        else:
            self.sock = None
            self.p = subprocess.Popen(["qrexec-client-vm", vm, "admin.vm.Console"],
                                      stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                      stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
            self.rfd, self.wfd = self.p.stdout.fileno(), self.p.stdin.fileno()
            self.how = f"qrexec-client-vm {vm} admin.vm.Console (child pid {self.p.pid})"
        os.set_blocking(self.rfd, False)

    def send(self, s):
        data = s.encode()
        try:
            while data:
                n = os.write(self.wfd, data)
                data = data[n:]
        except OSError as e:
            raise ConsoleGone(f"write to the console failed: {e}")

    def _read(self):
        try:
            d = os.read(self.rfd, 65536)
        except BlockingIOError:
            return b""
        except OSError:
            d = b""
        if d == b"":
            self.eof = True
            return b""
        self.buf += d
        if len(self.buf) > BUF_CAP:
            self.buf = self.buf[-BUF_CAP:]
        self.rx_bytes += len(d)
        self.last_rx = time.time()
        if self.transcript:
            self.transcript.write(d)
            self.transcript.flush()
        return d

    def absorb(self):
        """Take whatever is waiting without blocking (the daemon's idle loop)."""
        while True:
            r, _, _ = select.select([self.rfd], [], [], 0)
            if not r or not self._read():
                return

    def pump(self, until=None, deadline=DEADLINE, stall=STALL, on_data=None):
        """Four exits, and the caller is told which: 'hit' the marker appeared, 'stall' nothing
        arrived for `stall`s, 'deadline', 'eof' the attach itself ended."""
        t0 = last = time.time()
        while True:
            if until and until.encode() in self.buf:
                return "hit"
            if self.eof:
                return "eof"
            now = time.time()
            if now - t0 > deadline:
                return "deadline"
            if now - last > stall:
                return "stall"
            r, _, _ = select.select([self.rfd], [], [], 0.2)
            if r:
                d = self._read()
                if d:
                    last = time.time()
                    if on_data:
                        on_data(d)

    def settle(self, quiet=None, deadline=15):
        """Read until the console has been silent for `quiet` seconds; KEEP the bytes."""
        quiet = QUIET if quiet is None else quiet
        t0 = last = time.time()
        while time.time() - t0 < deadline and not self.eof:
            r, _, _ = select.select([self.rfd], [], [], 0.2)
            if r and self._read():
                last = time.time()
                continue
            if time.time() - last > quiet:
                break

    def drain_quiet(self, quiet=None, deadline=15):
        """Read until the console has been silent for `quiet` seconds, then discard.

        REQUIRED between exchanges. Syncing on a prompt character instead was the bug that made
        the first real run of this tool silently skip its command: pump(until='>') matched a
        prompt still trickling in from the PREVIOUS exchange. Sync on silence, and on the token
        itself - never on '>'."""
        self.settle(quiet, deadline)
        self.buf = b""

    def exit_code(self):
        return self.p.poll() if self.p else None

    def stderr_text(self):
        if not self.p:
            return ""
        try:
            os.set_blocking(self.p.stderr.fileno(), False)
            return (self.p.stderr.read() or b"").decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
        except Exception:
            return ""

    def close(self):
        try:
            if self.sock:
                self.sock.close()
            if self.p:
                self.p.kill()
                self.p.wait(timeout=5)
        except Exception:
            pass


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- shared steps
def classify_tail(buf):
    tail = buf[-300:]
    last = buf.split(b"\n")[-1]
    if b"login:" in last or b"login:" in buf[-40:]:
        return "login"
    if b"assword" in tail and b">" not in tail:
        return "password"
    if b">" in tail:
        return "shell"
    return "attached-guest-silent"


def wake(c):
    """Send the bare CR a fresh pty needs (no scrollback) and classify what came back.
    Returns (rc, phase, message). rc 0 means a usable session; the attach may be KEPT even when
    rc != 0 - the caller decides by `phase` ('dead' means nothing is attached any more)."""
    c.send("\r")
    why = c.pump(until="\n", deadline=8, stall=6)
    # The first newline is usually dom0's "[ATTACHED]" banner, which arrives BEFORE the guest
    # answers the CR - classifying on it alone reads a healthy login prompt as "guest silent"
    # (caught by the self-test on 2026-09-17). Let the answer finish arriving: settle on silence.
    if c.buf:
        c.settle(deadline=6)
    if not c.buf:
        rc, err = c.exit_code(), c.stderr_text()
        if rc == 200:
            return RC_BUSY, "dead", ("BUSY - another attacher holds the console lock (dom0 `xl "
                                     "console`, or a stale lock from a killed client)")
        if rc == 126:
            return RC_REFUSED, "dead", f"REFUSED by qrexec policy - admin.vm.Console not granted. {err}"
        if rc is not None or why == "eof":
            return RC_NOCONSOLE, "dead", (f"NOCONSOLE - the attach ENDED with no bytes at all "
                                          f"(child rc={rc} {err!r}); nothing is attached now")
        # NOT EVEN [ATTACHED] IS A STRONGER RESULT THAN "quiet". dom0 prints "[ATTACHED]" as soon
        # as it binds the domain's console, BEFORE the guest writes anything (measured 2026-09-09:
        # healthy guest -> banner within seconds; parked wedge -> nothing, no other attacher).
        return RC_NOCONSOLE, "silent", (
            "NOCONSOLE - no bytes at all, not even dom0's [ATTACHED] banner, and the attach is "
            "still up. This points at the ATTACH, not at guest software; INCONCLUSIVE alone. "
            "The session is LEFT OPEN - a silent session is information; re-attaching is "
            "forbidden. Check: 1. another attacher? (dom0 `xl console` splits the pty) "
            "2. xencons bound in the guest? 3. guest wedged at high IRQL?")
    phase = classify_tail(c.buf)
    if phase == "login":
        return RC_NEEDS_LOGIN, "login", "console is at the login prompt"
    if phase == "shell":
        return RC_OK, "shell", "shell prompt seen"
    return RC_NOCONSOLE, phase, (f"attached ({len(c.buf)} bytes, pump exit {why}) but no login "
                                 f"prompt and no shell prompt yet; session LEFT OPEN")


def login(c, user, pw, ld=None):
    """PROVEN SEQUENCE (2026-09-06, re-measured 2026-09-09 on win11-nfy): the user name goes
    straight into the prompt that is already there - no extra CR, no wait for a `login:` that is
    already in the buffer (that wait was a guaranteed no-op that looked like synchronisation, and
    the CR before it made the guest emit a SECOND prompt). Generous waits: a Windows login takes
    seconds; the old 10 s "assword" wait expired and read as "the console rejects input".
    Returns (rc, phase, message); the session is kept whatever happens."""
    ld = LOGIN_DEADLINE if ld is None else ld
    c.send(user + "\r")
    if c.pump(until="assword", deadline=ld, stall=ld) != "hit":
        return RC_NEEDS_LOGIN, "login-sent", (f"no password prompt within {ld:.0f} s after the "
                                              "user name - session LEFT OPEN (see the transcript)")
    c.send((pw or "") + "\r")
    n0 = len(c.buf)
    t0 = time.time()
    why = "deadline"
    while True:
        left = ld - (time.time() - t0)
        if left <= 0:
            break
        why = c.pump(until=">", deadline=left, stall=min(4.0, left))
        if why == "hit":
            return RC_OK, "shell", "logged in - shell prompt seen"
        # A REJECTED credential is NOT silence. Measured 2026-09-17 on a healthy win11de-gwt: the
        # guest echoed the user name, printed "Password:", and answered the (wrong) password with a
        # FRESH login prompt - the old code waited the whole deadline and reported "no shell prompt
        # within 45 s", i.e. the same words a dead console gets. Only bytes AFTER the password count.
        if os.environ.get("QCON_DEFECT") != "rejected" and b"login:" in c.buf[n0:]:   # GUARD:rejected
            return RC_NEEDS_LOGIN, "login", (
                "credential REJECTED - the guest answered the password with a fresh login prompt "
                "(the console is NOT silent); session LEFT OPEN at the login prompt: "
                "`qcon login <vm> --user U --pass P` retries through THIS attach, no new attach")
        if why != "stall":
            break
    return RC_NEEDS_LOGIN, "password-sent", (f"no shell prompt within {ld:.0f} s after the "
                                             f"password (pump exit: {why}) - session LEFT OPEN")


def run_command(c, cmd, deadline, stall, out):
    """Type ONE command through the open session and stream its output to `out(text)` until the
    end marker. Returns (rc, message). Never closes anything.

    The token is built IN THE GUEST (`set QT=`), so the echoed input line can never contain the
    literal marker; the buffer is synced on the token's own echo, which cannot be left over from
    a previous exchange."""
    tok = os.urandom(4).hex().upper()
    c.drain_quiet()
    c.send(f"set QT={tok}\r")
    why = c.pump(until=tok, deadline=15, stall=10)
    if why == "eof":
        return RC_NOCONSOLE, "the attach ENDED (console EOF) while syncing the token"
    if why != "hit":
        return RC_NO_OUTPUT, (f"console did not echo the token within 10 s - input is not reaching "
                              f"the shell (pump exit: {why}); session LEFT OPEN")
    c.drain_quiet()
    c.send("echo B-%QT%&" + cmd + "&echo E-%QT%\r")
    bmark, emark = f"B-{tok}".encode(), f"E-{tok}".encode()
    st = {"started": False, "upto": 0, "first": True}
    dec = codecs.getincrementaldecoder("utf-8")("replace")

    def emit(raw, final=False):
        text = dec.decode(raw, final).replace("\r", "")
        if st["first"] and text:
            text = text.lstrip("\n")
            st["first"] = False
        if text:
            out(text)

    def on_data(_chunk):
        buf = c.buf
        if not st["started"]:
            i = buf.find(bmark)
            if i < 0:
                return
            st["started"], st["upto"] = True, i + len(bmark)
        e = buf.find(emark, st["upto"])
        if e >= 0:
            emit(buf[st["upto"]:e])
            st["upto"] = e
            return
        safe = len(buf) - len(emark) + 1          # hold back a partial end marker
        if safe > st["upto"]:
            emit(buf[st["upto"]:safe])
            st["upto"] = safe

    why = c.pump(until=f"E-{tok}", deadline=deadline, stall=stall, on_data=on_data)
    if st["started"]:
        e = c.buf.find(emark, st["upto"])
        emit(c.buf[st["upto"]:(e if e >= 0 else len(c.buf))], final=True)
    if why == "hit":
        return RC_OK, "ok"
    if why == "eof":
        return RC_NOCONSOLE, "the attach ENDED (console EOF) mid-command; nothing is attached now"
    quiet = stall if why == "stall" else deadline
    seen = "the begin marker came back, so the shell started the command, then its output stopped" \
        if st["started"] else "not even the begin marker came back - the shell did not start it"
    return RC_NO_OUTPUT, (f"no output in {quiet:.0f} s (pump exit: {why}; {seen}) - session LEFT "
                          "OPEN. A silent session is information; re-attaching is forbidden. "
                          "`qcon status` / `qcon shell` to look, `qcon close` when done")


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- state on disk
def state_dir(vm):
    return os.path.join(STATE_ROOT, f"qcon-{vm}")


def ledger(vm, kind, detail):
    """Every attach and detach, timestamped, in the session dir AND in a root ledger that
    survives `close` - so a second attach can never happen silently."""
    line = f"{ts()} {kind} vm={vm} pid={os.getpid()} {detail}\n"
    os.makedirs(STATE_ROOT, exist_ok=True)
    for path in (os.path.join(STATE_ROOT, "qcon-attach-ledger.log"),
                 os.path.join(state_dir(vm), "attach.log")):
        try:
            with open(path, "a") as f:
                f.write(line)
        except OSError:
            pass


def read_state(sdir):
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(sdir, "state.json")) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except Exception:
        return None


def pid_is_daemon(pid):
    """True only for a LIVE qcon daemon: pid reuse is not a session, and neither is a zombie
    (os.kill(pid, 0) succeeds on a zombie - the one-shot path's own child - which made `close`
    think the daemon had survived; caught by the self-test 2026-09-17)."""
    try:
        os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)          # reap it if it is our child; else ChildProcessError
    except (ChildProcessError, OSError):
        pass
    try:
        with open(f"/proc/{pid}/stat") as f:
            if f.read().split(")")[-1].split()[0] == "Z":
                return False
        with open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb") as f:
            return b"_daemon" in f.read()
    except OSError:
        return False


def wait_gone(pid, seconds):
    t0 = time.time()
    while pid and time.time() - t0 < seconds and pid_is_daemon(pid):
        time.sleep(0.05)
    return not (pid and pid_is_daemon(pid))


def session_live(sdir):
    """(live, state). Live = the daemon pid exists AND is a qcon daemon."""
    st = read_state(sdir)
    if not os.path.isdir(sdir):
        return False, None
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(sdir, "pid")) as f:
            live = pid_is_daemon(int(f.read().strip()))
    except Exception:
        live = False
    return live, st


def describe_holder(st):
    if not st:
        return "unknown holder"
    return (f"opened {st.get('opened_at', '?')} by {st.get('holder', '?')}; daemon pid "
            f"{st.get('pid', '?')}; phase {st.get('phase', '?')}; last console activity "
            f"{st.get('last_rx', 'never')}")


def archive_and_remove(vm, sdir, op):
    src = os.path.join(sdir, "session.log")
    dst = os.path.join(STATE_ROOT, f"qcon-{vm}.closed.log")
    try:
        if os.path.exists(src):
            shutil.move(src, dst)
            say(op, f"transcript kept as {dst}")
    except OSError as e:
        say(op, f"could not keep the transcript: {e}")
    shutil.rmtree(sdir, ignore_errors=True)


def request(sdir, obj, on_out=None):
    """One request to the session daemon; streams {"out":..} lines to on_out, returns the final
    {"done":true,...} object, or None if the daemon went away."""
    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    s.connect(os.path.join(sdir, "sock"))
    s.sendall(json.dumps(obj).encode() + b"\n")
    f = s.makefile("rb")
    try:
        for line in f:
            try:
                o = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if "out" in o and on_out:
                on_out(o["out"])
            if o.get("done"):
                return o
    finally:
        f.close()
        s.close()
    return None


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- the daemon
class Daemon:
    """Holds THE attach for one guest. Bind the socket first (so the client can queue its
    wait_open), then attach/wake/login, then serve requests one at a time until `close`."""

    def __init__(self, vm, sdir, holder):
        self.vm, self.sdir, self.holder = vm, sdir, holder
        self.opened_at, self.opened_epoch = ts(), time.time()
        self.phase, self.open_rc, self.open_msg = "attaching", None, ""
        self.runs, self.c = 0, None
        self.dlog = open(os.path.join(sdir, "daemon.log"), "a")
        self.transcript = open(os.path.join(sdir, "session.log"), "ab")
        with open(os.path.join(sdir, "pid"), "w") as f:
            f.write(str(os.getpid()))
        self.ls = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
        self.ls.bind(os.path.join(sdir, "sock"))
        self.ls.listen(8)
        self.write_state()

    def log(self, op, msg):
        self.dlog.write(f"{ts()} [{op}] {msg}\n")
        self.dlog.flush()

    def write_state(self):
        st = {"vm": self.vm, "pid": os.getpid(), "holder": self.holder,
              "opened_at": self.opened_at, "opened_epoch": self.opened_epoch,
              "phase": self.phase, "runs": self.runs,
              "transport": self.c.how if self.c else TRANSPORT,
              "attached_at": (time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(self.c.attached_at))
                              if self.c else None),
              "last_rx": (time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(self.c.last_rx))
                          if self.c and self.c.last_rx else None),
              "rx_bytes": self.c.rx_bytes if self.c else 0,
              "open_rc": self.open_rc, "open_msg": self.open_msg}
        tmp = os.path.join(self.sdir, "state.json.tmp")
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            json.dump(st, f, indent=1)
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(self.sdir, "state.json"))
        return st

    def open_sequence(self, user, pw):
        ledger(self.vm, "ATTACH", f"op=open transport={TRANSPORT} holder={self.holder!r}")
        self.log("open", f"attaching via {TRANSPORT}")
        try:
            self.c = Console(self.vm, self.transcript)
        except Exception as e:
            self.open_rc, self.phase, self.open_msg = RC_NOCONSOLE, "dead", f"attach failed: {e}"
            ledger(self.vm, "DETACH", f"op=open reason=attach-failed {e!r}")
            self.write_state()
            return
        self.log("open", f"attached: {self.c.how}; waking with CR")
        try:
            rc, phase, msg = wake(self.c)
            if phase == "login" and user:
                self.log("open", f"login prompt seen; logging in as {user}")
                rc, phase, msg = login(self.c, user, pw)
            elif phase == "login":
                msg = "NEEDS_LOGIN - at the login prompt and no credentials given; session LEFT " \
                      "OPEN: `qcon login <vm> --user U --pass P` finishes it through THIS attach"
        except ConsoleGone as e:
            rc, phase, msg = RC_NOCONSOLE, "dead", str(e)
        self.open_rc, self.phase, self.open_msg = rc, phase, msg
        if phase == "dead":
            ledger(self.vm, "DETACH", f"op=open reason={msg!r}")
            self.c.close()
        self.log("open", f"rc={rc} phase={phase}: {msg}")
        self.write_state()

    # ---- request handlers --------------------------------------------------------------
    def reply(self, cl, **obj):
        try:
            cl.sendall(json.dumps(obj).encode() + b"\n")
        except OSError:
            pass

    def mark_dead(self, reason):
        if self.phase != "dead":
            self.phase = "dead"
            ledger(self.vm, "DETACH", f"reason={reason!r}")
            self.log("session", f"attach ended: {reason}")
            self.c.close()
            self.write_state()

    def h_run(self, cl, req):
        cmd = req.get("cmd", "")
        deadline, stall = float(req.get("deadline", DEADLINE)), float(req.get("stall", STALL))
        self.log("run", f"cmd={cmd!r} deadline={deadline} stall={stall}")
        if self.phase == "dead":
            return self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_NOCONSOLE,
                              msg="the attach has ENDED (see status/daemon.log); nothing is "
                                  "attached. `qcon close` to clean up; a new `open` is a NEW "
                                  "attach and is recorded as one")
        if self.phase in ("login", "login-sent", "password-sent"):
            return self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_NEEDS_LOGIN,
                              msg=f"NEEDS_LOGIN (phase {self.phase}) - the console is not at a "
                                  "shell; `qcon login <vm> --user U --pass P` through this session")
        self.runs += 1
        try:
            rc, msg = run_command(self.c, cmd, deadline, stall,
                                  lambda text: self.reply(cl, out=text))
        except ConsoleGone as e:
            rc, msg = RC_NOCONSOLE, str(e)
        if rc == RC_NOCONSOLE:
            self.mark_dead(msg)
        self.log("run", f"rc={rc}: {msg}")
        self.write_state()
        self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=rc, msg=msg)

    def h_login(self, cl, req):
        user, pw = req.get("user"), req.get("pass")
        self.log("login", f"user={user}")
        if self.phase == "dead":
            return self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_NOCONSOLE, msg="the attach has ENDED")
        if not user:
            return self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_USAGE, msg="--user is required")
        try:
            self.c.drain_quiet()
            rc, phase, msg = login(self.c, user, pw)
        except ConsoleGone as e:
            rc, phase, msg = RC_NOCONSOLE, "dead", str(e)
        self.phase = phase
        if phase == "dead":
            self.mark_dead(msg)
        self.log("login", f"rc={rc} phase={phase}: {msg}")
        self.write_state()
        self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=rc, msg=msg)

    def h_status(self, cl, _req):
        st = self.write_state()
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(self.sdir, "session.log"), "rb") as f:
                f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
                n = f.tell()
                f.seek(max(0, n - 400))
                st["tail"] = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
        except OSError:
            st["tail"] = ""
        self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_OK, msg="open", state=st)

    def h_shell(self, cl, _req):
        """Interactive passthrough on THE attach: console bytes -> client, client bytes ->
        console. Ends when the client hangs up. Starts by replaying the transcript's tail."""
        self.log("shell", "passthrough begins")
        if self.phase == "dead":
            cl.sendall(b"qcon shell: the attach has ENDED; nothing to talk to\r\n")
            return
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(self.sdir, "session.log"), "rb") as f:
                f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
                n = f.tell()
                f.seek(max(0, n - 4096))
                cl.sendall(b"---- transcript tail ----\r\n" + f.read() + b"\r\n---- live ----\r\n")
        except OSError:
            pass
        cl.setblocking(False)
        try:
            while not self.c.eof:
                r, _, _ = select.select([self.c.rfd, cl], [], [], 1.0)
                if self.c.rfd in r:
                    d = self.c._read()
                    if d:
                        cl.sendall(d)
                if cl in r:
                    try:
                        d = cl.recv(4096)
                    except BlockingIOError:
                        continue
                    if not d:
                        break
                    self.c.send(d.decode("utf-8", "replace"))
        except (OSError, ConsoleGone) as e:
            self.log("shell", f"ended: {e}")
        if self.c.eof:
            self.mark_dead("console EOF during shell")
        else:
            self.phase = classify_tail(self.c.buf)
        self.log("shell", f"passthrough ends; phase now {self.phase}")
        self.write_state()

    def h_close(self, cl, req):
        self.log("close", "closing the session")
        if self.phase != "dead":
            if req.get("logout"):
                try:
                    self.c.send("exit\r")
                    self.c.pump(until="login:", deadline=5, stall=3)
                except ConsoleGone:
                    pass
            self.phase = "closed"
            self.c.close()
            ledger(self.vm, "DETACH", "op=close reason=closed-by-client")
        self.write_state()
        self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_OK, msg="detached; session closed")
        return "exit"

    def handle(self, cl):
        cl.settimeout(30)
        raw = b""
        try:
            while not raw.endswith(b"\n"):
                d = cl.recv(1)
                if not d:
                    return None
                raw += d
            req = json.loads(raw)
        except Exception as e:
            self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_USAGE, msg=f"bad request: {e}")
            return None
        cl.settimeout(None)
        op = req.get("op")
        if op == "wait_open":
            self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=self.open_rc, msg=self.open_msg, phase=self.phase)
            return "exit" if self.phase == "dead" else None    # nothing attached: nothing to hold
        h = {"run": self.h_run, "login": self.h_login, "status": self.h_status,
             "shell": self.h_shell, "close": self.h_close}.get(op)
        if not h:
            self.reply(cl, done=True, rc=RC_USAGE, msg=f"unknown op {op!r}")
            return None
        return h(cl, req)

    def serve(self):
        while True:
            fds = [self.ls]
            if self.c and not self.c.eof and self.phase != "dead":
                fds.append(self.c.rfd)
            r, _, _ = select.select(fds, [], [], 1.0)
            if self.c and self.c.rfd in r:
                self.c.absorb()
                self.write_state()
            if self.c and self.phase != "dead":
                if self.c.eof:
                    self.mark_dead("console EOF while idle")
                elif self.c.exit_code() is not None:
                    self.mark_dead(f"console child exited rc={self.c.exit_code()} "
                                   f"{self.c.stderr_text()!r}")
            if self.ls in r:
                cl, _ = self.ls.accept()
                try:
                    verdict = self.handle(cl)
                finally:
                    try:
                        cl.close()
                    except OSError:
                        pass
                if verdict == "exit":
                    return

    def shutdown(self, reason):
        if self.c and self.phase not in ("dead", "closed"):
            self.phase = "dead"
            ledger(self.vm, "DETACH", f"reason={reason!r}")
            self.c.close()
            self.write_state()
        self.log("daemon", f"exit: {reason}")
        for p in ("sock", "pid"):
            try:
                os.unlink(os.path.join(self.sdir, p))
            except OSError:
                pass


def daemon_main(vm, sdir, holder):
    _install_signal_net(0)               # signals -> SystemExit -> finally (no alarm: it holds)
    d = Daemon(vm, sdir, holder)
    reason = "served close"
    try:
        d.open_sequence(os.environ.get("QCON_USER"), os.environ.get("QCON_PASS"))
        d.serve()
    except SystemExit as e:
        reason = f"signal/exit {e.code}"
        raise
    except Exception as e:
        reason = f"daemon crashed: {e!r}"
        raise
    finally:
        d.shutdown(reason)
    return 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- client verbs
def holder_string():
    ppid = os.getppid()
    try:
        with open(f"/proc/{ppid}/cmdline", "rb") as f:
            cmd = f.read().replace(b"\0", b" ").decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()[:120]
    except OSError:
        cmd = "?"
    try:
        tty = os.ttyname(0)
    except OSError:
        tty = "notty"
    return f"pid={os.getpid()} ppid={ppid} ppid_cmd={cmd!r} tty={tty}"


def cmd_open(vm, user, pw, op="open"):
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    live, st = session_live(sdir)
    if live:
        say(op, f"REFUSED - a session for {vm} is ALREADY OPEN and the console admits ONE "
                f"attacher: {describe_holder(st)}. Use `qcon run {vm} '<cmd>'`, `qcon status {vm}`"
                f" or `qcon close {vm}`; never a second attach")
        return RC_SESSION_EXISTS
    if os.path.isdir(sdir):
        say(op, f"previous session had ended ({describe_holder(st)}); its state is archived, "
                "and this open is a NEW attach (recorded in the ledger)")
        archive_and_remove(vm, sdir, op)
    if DEFECT == "perattach":
        os.makedirs(sdir, exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(sdir, "creds.json"), "w") as f:
            json.dump({"user": user, "pass": pw}, f)
        say(op, "DEFECT KNOB perattach: NOT attaching now - every `run` will attach by itself "
                "(the OLD attach-per-command behaviour, re-introduced for the self-test)")
        return RC_OK
    if not TRANSPORT.startswith("fake:") and vm_running(vm) is False:
        say(op, f"{vm} is not Running - a halted guest has no console")
        return RC_NOT_RUNNING
    os.makedirs(sdir, exist_ok=True)
    env = dict(os.environ)
    if user:
        env["QCON_USER"] = user
    if pw is not None:
        env["QCON_PASS"] = pw
    say(op, f"attaching ONCE to {vm} (transport {TRANSPORT}); state in {sdir}")
    with open(os.path.join(sdir, "daemon.log"), "ab") as dl:
        subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "_daemon", vm, sdir,
                          holder_string()],
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=dl, stderr=dl,
                         start_new_session=True, env=env, close_fds=True)
    sock = os.path.join(sdir, "sock")
    t0 = time.time()
    while not os.path.exists(sock) and time.time() - t0 < 10:
        time.sleep(0.05)
    try:
        r = request(sdir, {"op": "wait_open"})
    except OSError as e:
        r = None
        say(op, f"could not reach the session daemon: {e}")
    if r is None:
        say(op, f"the session daemon died during open - see {os.path.join(sdir, 'daemon.log')}")
        return RC_NOCONSOLE
    say(op, f"rc={r.get('rc')} phase={r.get('phase')}: {r.get('msg')}")
    if r.get("phase") == "dead":
        # Nothing is attached and the daemon is exiting. Keep nothing but the ledger.
        st = read_state(sdir) or {}
        wait_gone(st.get("pid"), 3)
        archive_and_remove(vm, sdir, op)
    return int(r.get("rc", RC_NOCONSOLE))


def require_session(vm, op):
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    live, st = session_live(sdir)
    if live:
        return sdir
    if os.path.isdir(sdir):
        say(op, f"the session for {vm} has ENDED ({describe_holder(st)}); `qcon close {vm}` "
                "cleans it up. No implicit attach")
    else:
        say(op, f"no session open for {vm} - `qcon open {vm} [--user U --pass P]` first. "
                "This verb NEVER attaches by itself")
    return None


def cmd_run(vm, cmd, deadline, stall, user, pw):
    op = "run"
    if DEFECT == "perattach":
        return run_perattach(vm, cmd, deadline, stall, user, pw)
    sdir = require_session(vm, op)
    if not sdir:
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    try:
        r = request(sdir, {"op": "run", "cmd": cmd, "deadline": deadline, "stall": stall},
                    on_out=lambda t: (sys.stdout.write(t), sys.stdout.flush()))
    except OSError as e:
        say(op, f"could not reach the session daemon: {e}")
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    if r is None:
        say(op, "the session daemon went away mid-command; `qcon status` / `qcon close`")
        return RC_NOCONSOLE
    rc = int(r.get("rc", RC_NOCONSOLE))
    if rc != RC_OK:
        say(op, f"rc={rc}: {r.get('msg')}")
    return rc


def run_perattach(vm, cmd, deadline, stall, user, pw):
    """THE OLD BEHAVIOUR, kept only so the self-test can watch it fail: attach for this command
    alone, wake, log in, run, detach. Against a console that serves one attach, the SECOND
    command returns nothing - the shape that lost specimen 10."""
    op = "run"
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(sdir, "creds.json")) as f:
            cr = json.load(f)
            user, pw = user or cr.get("user"), pw if pw is not None else cr.get("pass")
    except OSError:
        pass
    say(op, "DEFECT KNOB perattach: attaching for this command alone (the OLD behaviour)")
    ledger(vm, "ATTACH", f"op=run DEFECT=perattach cmd={cmd!r}")
    c = Console(vm)
    try:
        rc, phase, msg = wake(c)
        if phase == "login" and user:
            rc, phase, msg = login(c, user, pw)
        if phase not in ("shell",):
            say(op, f"rc={rc} phase={phase}: {msg} [perattach: this attach is DETACHED now, "
                    "as the old tool did]")
            return rc
        rc, msg = run_command(c, cmd, deadline, stall,
                              lambda t: (sys.stdout.write(t), sys.stdout.flush()))
        if rc != RC_OK:
            say(op, f"rc={rc}: {msg}")
        return rc
    except ConsoleGone as e:
        say(op, f"rc={RC_NOCONSOLE}: {e}")
        return RC_NOCONSOLE
    finally:
        c.close()
        ledger(vm, "DETACH", "op=run DEFECT=perattach")


def cmd_login(vm, user, pw):
    op = "login"
    sdir = require_session(vm, op)
    if not sdir:
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    if not user:
        say(op, "--user U (and --pass P) required")
        return RC_USAGE
    r = request(sdir, {"op": "login", "user": user, "pass": pw})
    if r is None:
        say(op, "the session daemon went away")
        return RC_NOCONSOLE
    say(op, f"rc={r.get('rc')}: {r.get('msg')}")
    return int(r.get("rc", RC_NOCONSOLE))


def cmd_status(vm):
    op = "status"
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    live, st = session_live(sdir)
    if not live:
        if st:
            say(op, f"session for {vm} has ENDED (not open): {describe_holder(st)}; "
                    f"`qcon close {vm}` cleans up")
        else:
            say(op, f"no session open for {vm}")
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    try:
        r = request(sdir, {"op": "status"})
    except OSError as e:
        say(op, f"session daemon unreachable: {e}")
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    if r is None:
        say(op, "session daemon went away")
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    s = r.get("state", {})
    try:
        age = f"{time.time() - float(s.get('opened_epoch')):.0f} s"
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        age = "?"
    print(f"qcon status: {vm}: OPEN phase={s.get('phase')} age={age} opened_at={s.get('opened_at')} "
          f"runs={s.get('runs')} rx_bytes={s.get('rx_bytes')} last_activity={s.get('last_rx') or 'never'}\n"
          f"qcon status: transport={s.get('transport')}\n"
          f"qcon status: holder={s.get('holder')} daemon_pid={s.get('pid')}\n"
          f"qcon status: open_rc={s.get('open_rc')} open_msg={s.get('open_msg')!r}\n"
          f"qcon status: transcript tail={s.get('tail', '')!r}\n"
          f"qcon status: state dir {sdir}")
    return RC_OK


def cmd_shell(vm, user, pw):
    op = "shell"
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    live, _ = session_live(sdir)
    if not live:
        rc = cmd_open(vm, user, pw, op="shell/open")
        live, _ = session_live(sdir)
        if not live:
            return rc
    say(op, "interactive passthrough on THE open session; lines you type go to the console "
            "(Enter -> CR); Ctrl-D ends the shell and LEAVES THE SESSION OPEN")
    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    s.connect(os.path.join(sdir, "sock"))
    s.sendall(json.dumps({"op": "shell"}).encode() + b"\n")
    stdin_fd = sys.stdin.fileno()
    eof_at = None                      # after stdin EOF, keep showing output until it goes quiet
    try:
        last = time.time()
        while True:
            r, _, _ = select.select([s] + ([] if eof_at else [stdin_fd]), [], [], 0.3)
            if s in r:
                d = s.recv(65536)
                if not d:
                    say(op, "the daemon ended the passthrough")
                    break
                last = time.time()
                sys.stdout.write(d.decode("utf-8", "replace"))
                sys.stdout.flush()
            if stdin_fd in r:
                line = os.read(stdin_fd, 4096)
                if not line:
                    eof_at = time.time()
                    continue
                s.sendall(line.replace(b"\n", b"\r"))
            if eof_at and (time.time() - last > 1.0 or time.time() - eof_at > 5.0):
                break
    finally:
        s.close()
    say(op, f"shell ended; the session for {vm} is still open (`qcon close {vm}` when done)")
    return RC_OK


def cmd_close(vm, logout=False):
    op = "close"
    sdir = state_dir(vm)
    live, st = session_live(sdir)
    if not os.path.isdir(sdir):
        say(op, f"no session open for {vm}")
        return RC_NO_SESSION
    if DEFECT == "perattach" and not live:
        shutil.rmtree(sdir, ignore_errors=True)
        say(op, "DEFECT KNOB perattach: nothing was held open; state removed")
        return RC_OK
    if not live:
        say(op, f"session had already ENDED ({describe_holder(st)}); removing its state")
        archive_and_remove(vm, sdir, op)
        return RC_OK
    try:
        pid = int(st.get("pid"))
    except Exception:
        pid = None
    try:
        r = request(sdir, {"op": "close", "logout": logout})
        say(op, f"rc={r.get('rc') if r else '?'}: {r.get('msg') if r else 'daemon went away'}")
    except OSError as e:
        say(op, f"daemon unreachable ({e}); terminating it")
    if not wait_gone(pid, 5):
        say(op, f"daemon {pid} still alive after close; sending SIGTERM (its finally detaches)")
        try:
            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
        except OSError:
            pass
        wait_gone(pid, 3)
    archive_and_remove(vm, sdir, op)
    say(op, f"session for {vm} closed; state removed")
    return RC_OK


def cmd_oneshot(vm, cmd, deadline, stall, user, pw):
    """open + run + close = ONE attach. Refused while a session exists (never a second attach)."""
    live, st = session_live(state_dir(vm))
    if live:
        say("open", f"REFUSED - a session for {vm} is already open ({describe_holder(st)}); "
                    f"use `qcon run {vm} '<cmd>'` through it")
        return RC_SESSION_EXISTS
    rc = cmd_open(vm, user, pw)
    try:
        if rc != RC_OK:
            return rc
        return cmd_run(vm, cmd, deadline, stall, user, pw)
    finally:
        if os.path.isdir(state_dir(vm)):
            cmd_close(vm)


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- argv
def parse(argv):
    """<verb> <vm> [options] [command] - options may appear anywhere after the verb."""
    opts = {"user": os.environ.get("QCON_USER"), "pass": os.environ.get("QCON_PASS"),
            "deadline": DEADLINE, "stall": STALL, "logout": False}
    rest = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("--user", "--pass", "--deadline", "--stall"):
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise ValueError(f"{a} needs a value")
            v = argv[i + 1]
            opts[a[2:]] = float(v) if a in ("--deadline", "--stall") else v
            i += 2
        elif a == "--logout":
            opts["logout"] = True
            i += 1
        else:
            rest.append(a)
            i += 1
    return opts, rest


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if len(argv) >= 4 and argv[0] == "_daemon":
        return daemon_main(argv[1], argv[2], argv[3])
    if not argv:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    verbs = ("open", "run", "login", "status", "shell", "close")
    try:
        if argv[0] in verbs:
            verb = argv[0]
            o, rest = parse(argv[1:])
        else:
            verb = "oneshot"
            o, rest = parse(argv)
    except ValueError as e:
        say("usage", str(e))
        return RC_USAGE
    if not rest:
        say("usage", "a <vm> is required")
        return RC_USAGE
    vm, args = rest[0], rest[1:]
    if verb == "open":
        return cmd_open(vm, o["user"], o["pass"])
    if verb == "run":
        if not args:
            say("run", "a '<command>' is required")
            return RC_USAGE
        return cmd_run(vm, " ".join(args), o["deadline"], o["stall"], o["user"], o["pass"])
    if verb == "login":
        return cmd_login(vm, o["user"], o["pass"])
    if verb == "status":
        return cmd_status(vm)
    if verb == "shell":
        return cmd_shell(vm, o["user"], o["pass"])
    if verb == "close":
        return cmd_close(vm, o["logout"])
    if not args:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    return cmd_oneshot(vm, " ".join(args), o["deadline"], o["stall"], o["user"], o["pass"])


if __name__ == "__main__":
    _install_signal_net(BUDGET)
    sys.exit(main())
